    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Ranunculus gramineus</b></i>, called the <b>grass-leaved buttercup</b>, is a species of flowering plant in the genus <i>Ranunculus</i>, native to the western Mediterranean; Morocco, Algeria, Tunisia, Portugal, Spain, France, Italy (including Sardinia), and Switzerland. It has gained the Royal Horticultural Society's Award of Garden Merit.",
